test(backend-readiness): align claude-cli expectations with new policy

Commit 2ee5976a ("fix(telemetry): allow claude-cli backend through
fail-closed gate") added a `case 'claude-cli'` branch to
assessBackendTelemetryPolicy that allows launch when the model has an
exact MODEL_RATES entry. The default Claude model satisfies this, so
the readiness summary no longer picks up the telemetry-blocked tail.

The existing test "keeps claude-cli probe details while still blocking
launch under telemetry policy" was written against the old default-
blocked behavior and now fails on every CI matrix slot.

Update:
- Rename the original test to "keeps claude-cli probe details when
  binary missing (telemetry policy allows the default model)" and
  assert the summary does NOT contain "blocked until exact token
  counts" (the new contract).
- Add a new test "claude-cli with an unknown model still blocks
  launch under telemetry policy" that passes a fabricated model
  string with no MODEL_RATES entry, exercising the still-blocked path
  and asserting "no exact cost rate entry" appears in the summary.

Validation: 5427/5428 unit tests pass locally (1 pre-existing skip);
backend-readiness.test.js is green for both new and existing
claude-cli tests.

Out of scope: changing the policy itself (already correct in 2ee5976a)
or adding aliases (already covered by 1459c0d4).


